# Wrong proofs that a checker must reject. Most come from the probes run
# against the 2018 engine on 2026-10-26. The format is described in ../README.md.

# --- Notation ---

case: negation-symbol
source: soundness probe
problem: {¬P=>P}
2. P ; 1 DN
expect: invalid at 2: ¬ is negation, so DN turns ¬P into ~~~P, not into P
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 parser drops ¬ and reads ¬P as P

# --- Rules of inference ---

case: mt-wrong-consequent
source: soundness probe
problem: {A → B//~C=>~A}
3. ~A ; 1,2 MT
expect: invalid at 3: MT needs ~B, the negation of the consequent B
argument: invalid
legacy: MT only checks that one of the two cited lines is a negation

case: mt-denying-the-antecedent
source: soundness, classic fallacy
problem: {P → Q//~P=>~Q}
3. ~Q ; 1,2 MT
expect: invalid at 3: MT needs ~Q, the negation of the consequent, and gives ~P
argument: invalid

case: mp-affirming-the-consequent
source: soundness, classic fallacy
problem: {P → Q//Q=>P}
3. P ; 1,2 MP
expect: invalid at 3: MP needs the antecedent P and gives the consequent Q
argument: invalid

case: ds-wrong-disjunct
source: soundness probe
problem: {A | B//~C=>B}
3. B ; 1,2 DS
expect: invalid at 3: DS needs ~A, the negation of a disjunct
argument: invalid
legacy: DS only checks that one of the two cited lines is a negation

case: cd-backwards
source: soundness
problem: {(A → B) & (C → D)//B | D=>A | C}
3. A | C ; 1,2 CD
expect: invalid at 3: CD needs A | C and gives B | D
argument: invalid

case: simp-from-disjunction
source: soundness
problem: {P | Q=>P}
2. P ; 1 SIMP
expect: invalid at 2: SIMP needs a conjunction
argument: invalid

case: mp-repeats-a-line
source: soundness probe
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P ; 1,2 MP
4. P & Q ; 3,2 CONJ
expect: invalid at 3: MP needs a conditional, and neither P nor Q is one
legacy: a rule that does not apply returns its input unchanged, so any rule can repeat a line

# --- Rules of replacement ---

case: dist-no-common-factor
source: soundness probe
problem: {P | (Q | R)=>(P | Q) & (P | R)}
2. (P | Q) & (P | R) ; 1 DIST
expect: invalid at 2: DIST needs p | (q & r), and Q | R is not a conjunction
argument: invalid
legacy: DIST does not check the inner connective

case: dist-different-factors
source: soundness probe
problem: {(P | Q) & (R | S)=>P | (Q & S)}
2. P | (Q & S) ; 1 DIST
expect: invalid at 2: DIST needs a common disjunct, and P | Q and R | S share none
argument: invalid
legacy: DIST does not check that both sides share a factor

case: exp-on-disjunction
source: soundness probe
problem: {(P & Q) | R=>P → (Q → R)}
2. P → (Q → R) ; 1 EXP
expect: invalid at 2: EXP needs (p & q) → r, and line 1 is a disjunction
argument: invalid
legacy: EXP does not check that the formula is a conditional

case: exp-on-disjunction-2
source: soundness probe
problem: {P | (Q → R)=>(P & Q) → R}
2. (P & Q) → R ; 1 EXP
expect: invalid at 2: EXP needs p → (q → r), and line 1 is a disjunction
argument: invalid
legacy: EXP does not check that the formula is a conditional

case: exp-on-wrong-antecedent
source: soundness
problem: {(P | Q) → R=>P → (Q → R)}
2. P → (Q → R) ; 1 EXP
expect: invalid at 2: EXP needs a conjunction as antecedent, and P | Q is a disjunction

case: com-on-conditional
source: soundness, converse of a conditional
problem: {P → Q=>Q → P}
2. Q → P ; 1 COM
expect: invalid at 2: COM does not apply to →
argument: invalid

case: assoc-mixed-connectives
source: soundness
problem: {P & (Q | R)=>(P & Q) | R}
2. (P & Q) | R ; 1 ASSOC
expect: invalid at 2: ASSOC needs the same connective twice

case: trans-without-swap
source: soundness, inverse of a conditional
problem: {P → Q=>~P → ~Q}
2. ~P → ~Q ; 1 TRANS
expect: invalid at 2: TRANS gives ~Q → ~P
argument: invalid

case: impl-without-negation
source: soundness
problem: {P → Q=>P | Q}
2. P | Q ; 1 IMPL
expect: invalid at 2: IMPL gives ~P | Q
argument: invalid

case: dm-keeps-the-connective
source: soundness
problem: {~(P & Q)=>~P & ~Q}
2. ~P & ~Q ; 1 DM
expect: invalid at 2: DM gives ~P | ~Q
argument: invalid

case: equiv-one-direction
source: soundness
problem: {P ↔ Q=>P → Q}
2. P → Q ; 1 EQUIV
expect: invalid at 2: EQUIV gives (P → Q) & (Q → P); taking one conditional is a SIMP step

case: taut-different-conjuncts
source: soundness
problem: {P & Q=>P}
2. P ; 1 TAUT
expect: invalid at 2: TAUT needs p & p or p | p

# --- Proof structure ---

case: garbage-after-conclusion
source: soundness probe
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P & Q ; 1,2 CONJ
4. Z ; 1 MP
expect: invalid at 4: MP needs two lines, a conditional and its antecedent
legacy: the 2018 engine stops checking at the first line equal to the conclusion

case: conclusion-not-reached
source: soundness
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P | R ; 1 ADD
expect: invalid at end: the last line is P | R, and the conclusion is P & Q

case: cite-line-zero
source: soundness probe
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P & Q ; 0,2 CONJ
expect: invalid at 3: there is no line 0
legacy: crashes with IndexOutOfBoundsException

case: cite-later-line
source: soundness
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P & Q ; 1,4 CONJ
4. Q | R ; 2 ADD
expect: invalid at 3: a line can only cite earlier lines

case: cite-own-line
source: soundness
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P & Q ; 1,3 CONJ
expect: invalid at 3: a line can only cite earlier lines

case: too-few-citations
source: soundness probe
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P & Q ; 1 CONJ
expect: invalid at 3: CONJ cites two lines
legacy: crashes with IndexOutOfBoundsException

case: too-many-citations
source: soundness
problem: {P & Q//R=>P}
3. P ; 1,2 SIMP
expect: invalid at 3: SIMP cites one line
legacy: SIMP ignores the extra cited line

case: unknown-rule
source: soundness
problem: {P//Q=>P & Q}
3. P & Q ; 1,2 AND
expect: invalid at 3: there is no rule called AND

# --- Quantifiers ---

case: ug-from-constant
source: soundness probe
problem: {Fa=>(∀x)Fx}
2. (∀x)Fx ; 1 UG
expect: invalid at 2: UG generalizes a variable, and a is a constant
argument: invalid
legacy: UG generalizes constants

case: ug-after-ei
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∃x)Fx=>(∀x)Fx}
2. Fa ; 1 EI
3. (∀x)Fx ; 2 UG
expect: invalid at 3: UG generalizes a variable, and a is a constant
argument: invalid
legacy: UG generalizes constants

case: ug-after-ui-to-constant
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∀x)Fx=>(∀y)Fy}
2. Fa ; 1 UI
3. (∀y)Fy ; 2 UG
expect: invalid at 3: UG generalizes a variable, and a is a constant
legacy: UG generalizes constants

case: ug-variable-free-in-premise
source: soundness
problem: {Fx=>(∀x)Fx}
2. (∀x)Fx ; 1 UG
expect: invalid at 2: UG cannot generalize x, which is free in premise 1
argument: invalid
legacy: the 2018 engine lets UG generalize a variable that is free in a premise

case: ug-variable-free-in-ei-line
source: soundness, the classic quantifier swap fallacy
problem: {(∀y)(∃x)Lxy=>(∃x)(∀y)Lxy}
2. (∃x)Lxy ; 1 UI
3. Lay ; 2 EI
4. (∀y)Lay ; 3 UG
5. (∃x)(∀y)Lxy ; 4 EG
expect: invalid at 4: UG cannot generalize y, which is free in line 3, obtained by EI
argument: invalid
legacy: UG accepts any (∀y) put in front of a line; the engine does not track which lines come from EI

case: ug-leaves-a-free-occurrence
source: soundness
problem: {(∀x)Fxx=>(∀x)Fxy}
2. Fyy ; 1 UI
3. (∀x)Fxy ; 2 UG
expect: invalid at 3: UG must replace every free y, and (∀x)Fxy keeps one
argument: invalid

case: ei-constant-used-in-earlier-line
source: soundness probe, the classic EI fallacy
problem: {(∃x)Fx//(∃x)Gx=>(∃x)(Fx & Gx)}
3. Fa ; 1 EI
4. Ga ; 2 EI
5. Fa & Ga ; 3,4 CONJ
6. (∃x)(Fx & Gx) ; 5 EG
expect: invalid at 4: EI needs a new constant, and a occurs in line 3
argument: invalid

case: ei-constant-used-in-premise
source: soundness probe
problem: {Ga//(∃x)Fx=>(∃x)(Fx & Gx)}
3. Fa ; 2 EI
4. Fa & Ga ; 3,1 CONJ
5. (∃x)(Fx & Gx) ; 4 EG
expect: invalid at 3: EI needs a new constant, and a occurs in premise 1
argument: invalid

case: ei-constant-inside-nested-quantifier
source: soundness probe
problem: {P & (∀x)Hxa//(∃x)Fx=>(∃x)(Fx & Hxx)}
3. Fa ; 2 EI
4. (∀x)Hxa & P ; 1 COM
5. (∀x)Hxa ; 4 SIMP
6. Haa ; 5 UI
7. Fa & Haa ; 3,6 CONJ
8. (∃x)(Fx & Hxx) ; 7 EG
expect: invalid at 3: EI needs a new constant, and a occurs in premise 1, inside (∀x)Hxa
argument: invalid
legacy: EI does not look for the constant inside quantified subformulas

case: ei-to-variable
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∃x)Fx=>Fy}
2. Fy ; 1 EI
expect: invalid at 2: EI must use a constant, not the variable y
argument: invalid
legacy: EI accepts a variable

case: ui-capture
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∀x)(∃y)Lxy=>(∃y)Lyy}
2. (∃y)Lyy ; 1 UI
expect: invalid at 2: putting y for x puts it under (∃y), which captures it
argument: invalid
legacy: UI does not check for capture

case: ui-partial
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∀x)(Fx → Gx)=>Fa → Gx}
2. Fa → Gx ; 1 UI
expect: invalid at 2: UI must replace every free x
argument: invalid

case: ui-replaces-a-bound-occurrence
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∀x)(Fx → (∃x)Gx)=>Fa → (∃x)Ga}
2. Fa → (∃x)Ga ; 1 UI
expect: invalid at 2: the x in Gx is bound by (∃x), so UI must leave it alone
argument: invalid

case: ui-inside-a-line
source: soundness probe
problem: {P & (∀x)Fx=>P & Fa}
2. P & Fa ; 1 UI
expect: invalid at 2: UI applies to a whole line that starts with ∀

case: eg-capture
source: soundness
problem: {(∀y)Lay=>(∃y)(∀y)Lyy}
2. (∃y)(∀y)Lyy ; 1 EG
expect: invalid at 2: every y in (∀y)Lyy is bound by (∀y), so it is not an instance of line 1
argument: invalid
legacy: EG does not check whether an inner quantifier captures the new variable

case: quantifier-swap-by-repetition
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∃x)(∀y)Lxy//P=>(∃y)(∀x)Lxy}
3. (∃y)(∀x)Lxy ; 1,2 MP
expect: invalid at 3: MP needs a conditional, and (∃y)(∀x)Lxy is not (∃x)(∀y)Lxy
argument: invalid
legacy: a rule that does not apply returns its input unchanged, and the engine ignores which variable a quantifier binds

case: bound-variable-matters
source: soundness probe
problem: {(∀x)Fx//Q=>(∀y)Fx & Q}
3. (∀y)Fx & Q ; 1,2 CONJ
expect: invalid at 3: (∀y)Fx is not (∀x)Fx; its x is free
legacy: the 2018 engine ignores which variable a quantifier binds
